-- title:
--   A transversal of ±Γ in SL₂(ℤ) adapted to T and S
-- statement:
--   Let $\Gamma$ be a finite-index subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, and write $S$ and $T$ for the standard generators `ModularGroup.S` and `ModularGroup.T`. Assume that for every $j \in \mathbb Z$ neither $S T^j$ nor $-(S T^j)$ lies in $\Gamma$, and let $h_0$ be a natural number with $0 < h_0$ such that $T^{h_0} \in \Gamma$ or $-T^{h_0} \in \Gamma$, while for every natural $j$ with $0 < j < h_0$ neither $T^j$ nor $-T^j$ lies in $\Gamma$. Then there is a finite set $s$ of elements of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ with the following four properties: (i) every $g \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ satisfies $g x^{-1} \in \Gamma$ or $-(g x^{-1}) \in \Gamma$ for some $x \in s$; (ii) if $x, y \in s$ and $x y^{-1} \in \Gamma$ or $-(x y^{-1}) \in \Gamma$, then $x = y$; (iii) $T^j \in s$ for every natural $j < h_0$, and $S \in s$; (iv) every $x \in s$ which is not equal to any $T^j$ with $j < h_0$ and is not equal to $S$ satisfies: for all $j \in \mathbb Z$, neither $x T^j$ nor $-(x T^j)$ lies in $\Gamma$, and neither $x S^{-1}$ nor $-(x S^{-1})$ lies in $\Gamma$. Thus $s$ is a transversal for the right cosets of the group generated by $\Gamma$ and $-1$, containing the prescribed representatives $T^0, \dots, T^{h_0-1}, S$, with all remaining members lying in cosets distinct from those of all $T^j$ ($j \in \mathbb Z$) and of $S$.
--
--   This is the coset decomposition of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ by $\pm\Gamma$ organised according to cusps: the $h_0$ cosets $\pm\Gamma T^j$ lie over the cusp $\infty$ (whose width for $\Gamma$ is $h_0$), the coset $\pm\Gamma S$ lies over the cusp $0$, which the first hypothesis forces to be inequivalent to $\infty$, and the other representatives lie over cusps equivalent to neither. It is used in the computation of the leading $q$-expansion coefficients of a trace from level $\Gamma$ to level one, coset by coset, by [`ModularForm.qExpansion_slash_coeff_mem_of_peaked_auxiliary`](thm.html#ModularForm.qExpansion_slash_coeff_mem_of_peaked_auxiliary).
